To arrange an array in a wave-like pattern in Java, you can follow the approach of sorting the array first and then swapping adjacent elements.

i was able to answer this but i struggled when the array has duplicate elements

Input: [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5]
Expected Output: [2, 1, 3, 2, 5, 4] (or any other valid wave pattern like [2, 1, 4, 3, 5, 2])

import java.util.Arrays;

public class WaveArray {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5};
        waveSort(arr);
        System.out.println("Wave array: " + Arrays.toString(arr));
    }

    public static void waveSort(int[] arr) {
        Arrays.sort(arr); // Step 1: Sort the array

        // Step 2: Swap adjacent elements to create a wave
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i += 2) {
            // Swap arr[i] and arr[i+1]
            int temp = arr[i];
            arr[i] = arr[i + 1];
            arr[i + 1] = temp;
        }
    }
}


